    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="8084aa69-aee3-5597-aaac-f4d920fc41a4" activityNameId="c88a4ca3-f0f2-57d2-8ea1-f96617330415" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Scantling, softwood, laminated, CCF, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Scantling, softwood, laminated, CCF, at plant
The thickness of the scantling is 0.071m. The bill of materials is based on data from two scantling producers. Allocation of co-products is either based on physical properties (wood inputs) or economical properties (working materials, production loss). An unweighted average was calculated.;
UUID: fadf3875-ce14-3866-b7aa-c233a8084913
Included are the materials used in a laminated (C=continuous;F=finger-jointed) scantling. Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at scantling producers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fadf3875-ce14-3866-b7aa-c233a8084913.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
